  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY NIGHT THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 323 PM EDT Mon Jul 20 2026\n\nWednesday through Friday...\n\nThe current model consensus has the surface cold front pushing \nthrough south central and southeastern KY during the morning hours \non Wednesday, which may leave just enough forcing and low-level \nmoisture in place for an isolated shower or two south of the WK/BG \nParkways. Otherwise, the mid-to-late week period is expected to \nfeature dry weather and pleasant temperatures across the Ohio Valley \nand into the mid South. Upper-level troughing continuing to dig \nacross the eastern CONUS should help the sfc cold front push well to \nthe south of the area as 1020+ mb sfc high pressure settles into the \nregion from the north. The post-frontal air mass is expected to be \nquite refreshing given the recent prevalence of muggy weather, with \nECMWF ensemble mean PW values falling below 1\" (< 10th percentile of \nclimo) Wednesday night into Thursday. Temperatures are also expected \nto be below normal Wednesday through Friday, with highs in the upper \n70s and low-to-mid 80s with lows in the upper 50s and 60s.\n\nFriday Night into the Weekend...\n\nBy the end of the week, the upper level pattern will become more \nzonal, though broad NW flow should continue across the Ohio Valley. \nA subtle upper shortwave is expected to eject across the northern US \nRockies and into the Plains Thursday night into Friday before \ntracking toward our area Friday night. Ahead of this system, model \nguidance shows modest moisture return primarily into southern KY, \nwith PW values creeping back above 1.50\" later Friday into Saturday. \nWhile confidence is still low this far out, this could bring a \nreturn to isolated/scattered rain chances for the first part of the \nweekend. Behind this system, the broad upper ridge/heat dome across \nthe western US is expected to nudge slightly to the east, with \ntemperatures expected to trend back toward normal Sunday into early \nnext week. Mostly dry conditions are expected late weekend as \nseasonable moisture and weak forcing are favored at this time.",
